MaxOff patch of next@16.3.5 (v1.9, owner option (b) of 3 Nov 2026, issue #89 in prakyats/MaxOff).
pnpm applies everything from the first "diff --git" line down; this header is for people.

WHAT IT CHANGES (the same three edits in dist/client and dist/esm/client):
  segment-cache/navigation.js     navigateToKnownRoute keeps the navigation's scrollBehavior on its
                                  `accumulation`.
  router-reducer/ppr-navigations  spawnDynamicRequests -> finishNavigationTask ->
                                  dispatchRetryDueToTreeMismatch carry it onto the soft retry's
                                  ACTION_SERVER_PATCH action (`scrollBehavior`).
  reducers/server-patch-reducer   the retry navigates with NoScroll when the mismatched navigation
                                  asked for NoScroll (router.refresh(), scroll={false}); anything
                                  else (undefined: a normal navigation, a history restore) is
                                  ScrollBehavior.Default exactly as before.
Nothing else: no fetch, no history write, no hard-navigation rule is changed (two mismatches in a
row still fall back to an MPA navigation, as upstream).

REMOVE IT when upstream fixes the issue below. On every Next upgrade: pnpm refuses to install while
this names a version that is not installed, so drop the entry in pnpm-workspace.yaml, upgrade,
and run `pnpm exec playwright test e2e/view-scroll.spec.ts` (desktop, mobile, mobile-lg) with a
fresh build: green without the patch = fixed upstream, delete this file; red = re-make the patch
with `pnpm patch next@<version>` (check server-patch-reducer.js still hard-codes Default).

READY-TO-FILE UPSTREAM ISSUE (github.com/vercel/next.js/issues/new, "Bug report"):
  Title: router.refresh() scrolls to the top when its response mismatches the tree
         (server-patch retry ignores the refresh's NoScroll)
  Next.js: 16.3.5 (App Router, segment cache; also read in 16.3.8's source)
  Repro (minimal):
    1. app/page.tsx: a long page (height 3000px) with a client component that
       a) switches a view with `history.replaceState(null, "", "?tab=b")` (a view control that
          must not fetch), and b) has a button that calls `router.refresh()`.
    2. Load `/`, click the view switch (the URL is now `/?tab=b`), scroll to the bottom.
    3. Click "refresh".
    Expected: the page stays where it is (a refresh asks for ScrollBehavior.NoScroll).
    Actual: the page jumps to the top (document.documentElement.scrollTop = 0).
  Cause: after the hand-written replaceState the router "restores" with the tree it has, whose
    page segment is still keyed `__PAGE__`. The refresh's answer is keyed `__PAGE__?{"tab":"b"}`,
    so finishNavigationTask sees a tree mismatch and dispatchRetryDueToTreeMismatch sends
    ACTION_SERVER_PATCH. serverPatchReducer hard-codes `ScrollBehavior.Default`; in the retry the
    page segment differs by search params (segmentMatchKind 2), accumulateScrollRef assigns a
    ScrollRef, and the layout router scrolls. The refresh's NoScroll is lost on the retry.
  Suggested fix (this patch): carry the original navigation's scrollBehavior through
    spawnDynamicRequests/finishNavigationTask onto the retry action and use it in
    serverPatchReducer (NoScroll stays NoScroll, Default stays Default).
  Related, not changed here: two overlapping refreshes in that state both mismatch and the
    second becomes a hard (MPA) navigation via `previousNavigationDidMismatch`.

